ytdownloader (0.4.1-1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Root cause of the "title shows, controls vanish at completion" bug
    found and removed: the row's enabled-state toggling (setEnabled(False)
    on the progress bar and button when a download completes) triggered
    Qt/Wayland to composite a frame without those child widgets. Widgets
    are never enabled/disabled now; terminal rows are greyed with a
    cascading stylesheet and the pause/done button is a click-guarded
    no-op.
  * A one-second watchdog repaints the Downloads viewport synchronously,
    healing any residual compositor staleness within a second — the
    controls are guaranteed visible for every row in every state.

 -- User <user@example.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:30:00 +0000

ytdownloader (0.4.0-1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Downloads rows are now persistent widgets: created once per item, then
    updated in place — never torn down and recreated. This fixes the
    remaining stale-frame cases under Wayland where a finished download
    showed only its title until an expose event (e.g. switching
    workspaces) forced a redraw; the progress bar, percentage, Done and X
    now appear immediately.
  * Worker-derived titles no longer include the per-format suffix.

 -- User <user@example.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 16:30:00 +0000

ytdownloader (0.3.9-1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Fix rows rendering without their controls under Wayland: after a
    download starts/resumes (and after it completes) the compositor could
    keep showing a stale frame in which only the row label was painted —
    progress bar, ETA, Pause/Resume and X invisible until a mouse-over
    forced a redraw. Rows and the list viewport now repaint synchronously
    on every rebuild and state change, and progress ticks repaint their
    controls explicitly.

