ytdownloader (0.3.7-1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Duplicate detection is now canonical: desktop (www), mobile (m),
    youtu.be/ and /shorts/ links of the same video id are recognised as the
    same source (per format), not just the identical URL string.
  * Ceremony around the row-app acknowledgement window (end of download):
    instrumented reproduction of completion with delayed acknowledgement
    shows rows continuously present with progress bar, pause/resume and X
    across the whole window; no change required.

 -- User <user@example.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

ytdownloader (0.3.6-1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Same source may be downloaded in different formats: duplicate detection
    is keyed on (source URL, format). Audio and video of one URL are
    separate, independent downloads.
  * Filenames differ per format — outputs are "<title> [audio].<ext>" and
    "<title> [video].<ext>" — so the two formats of one source can never
    overwrite each other's existing or in-progress files.
  * Sources already queued/active (same format) are rejected with a notice;
    sources already downloaded earlier are confirmed by dialog before a
    re-download; previously failed sources ask before retrying.
  * Pausing and resuming no longer consume retry attempts.
  * Downloads-list rebuilds now skip no-op refreshes (state-signature
    comparison) so live rows are never torn down mid-download.
  * Terminal items are scrubbed from paused/retry pools (no ghost states).
  * The Download button no longer shows a tooltip.

 -- User <user@example.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:00:00 +0000

ytdownloader (0.3.5-1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Downloads rows now show the human-friendly video title instead of the
    URL (the URL moves into the row tooltip). Titles come from the validated
    input, or from yt-dlp output once a download starts.
  * Items restored from state without a title get one in the background
    (one lightweight yt-dlp lookup per item, serialised).
  * Fixed rows/controls sometimes disappearing when resuming, pausing or
    removing items: row list rebuilds are now deferred out of the click
    handler so a widget is never destroyed while its own slot is running;
    pause-from-row triggers the list refresh reliably.

